<template>
  <section>
    <h2 class="pdx-txt-heading section-heading">Live Demo</h2>
    <p class="pdx-txt-small pdx-ink-muted">Scroll the content below. The nav links highlight automatically.</p>
    <div class="spy-layout">
      <pdx-scroll-spy>
        <nav class="spy-nav">
          <a href="#spy-intro" data-spy-link data-spy-target="spy-intro" class="spy-link">Introduction</a>
          <a href="#spy-install" data-spy-link data-spy-target="spy-install" class="spy-link">Installation</a>
          <a href="#spy-usage" data-spy-link data-spy-target="spy-usage" class="spy-link">Usage</a>
          <a href="#spy-api" data-spy-link data-spy-target="spy-api" class="spy-link">API Reference</a>
          <a href="#spy-faq" data-spy-link data-spy-target="spy-faq" class="spy-link">FAQ</a>
        </nav>
        <div class="spy-content">
          <div data-section="spy-intro" id="spy-intro" class="spy-section">
            <h3>Introduction</h3>
            <p>ScrollSpy observes which section is currently in the viewport and highlights the corresponding navigation link. This is useful for long documentation pages, landing pages, and single-page navigation.</p>
            <p>The component uses IntersectionObserver for efficient, performant section detection — no scroll event polling.</p>
          </div>
          <div data-section="spy-install" id="spy-install" class="spy-section">
            <h3>Installation</h3>
            <p>Import the component from <code>@pdxui/ui</code>. It auto-registers as <code>&lt;pdx-scroll-spy&gt;</code>.</p>
            <p>Wrap your navigation links and content sections inside the component. Add <code>data-spy-link</code> to nav links and <code>data-section</code> to content sections.</p>
          </div>
          <div data-section="spy-usage" id="spy-usage" class="spy-section">
            <h3>Usage</h3>
            <p>Place <code>data-spy-target="sectionId"</code> on each link to match the section's <code>data-section</code> value. The component automatically adds an <code>active</code> class to the currently visible section's link.</p>
            <p>Clicking a link scrolls smoothly to the target section (configurable via <code>smoothscroll</code> prop).</p>
          </div>
          <div data-section="spy-api" id="spy-api" class="spy-section">
            <h3>API Reference</h3>
            <p>Configure the observation threshold with the <code>offset</code> prop. Customize selectors with <code>sectionselector</code> and <code>linkselector</code> props.</p>
            <p>The component emits a <code>pdx-change</code> event when the active section changes, with the section key in the event detail.</p>
          </div>
          <div data-section="spy-faq" id="spy-faq" class="spy-section">
            <h3>FAQ</h3>
            <p><strong>Q: Does it work with dynamic content?</strong><br/>A: Yes, the observer watches for DOM mutations and re-initializes automatically.</p>
            <p><strong>Q: Can I use custom selectors?</strong><br/>A: Yes, use the <code>sectionselector</code> and <code>linkselector</code> props.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </pdx-scroll-spy>
    </div>
